was so tight and i literally  could not breathe they may have looked  amazing but their experiences were worse  than you could imagine onset horror  stories about the wardrobe are all too  common you may see these actors in a  whole new light when you learn what they  went through to portray your favorite  characters  like i could i was absolutely blinded  tom holland looks great as spider-man  but he wasn't the most comfortable while  playing the web slinger the suit he wore  in homecoming was very restrictive  making it difficult to breathe zendaya  even said she was afraid the suit would  choke tom on top of this the suit made  it a hassle to drink water and use the  bathroom he had to drink through a straw  fed through one of his eye holes and had  to plan his bathroom breaks 45 minutes  in advance it looks amazing it feels  terrible black widow seems cool and  comfortable when she's taking down bad  guys but it was a different story for  scarlett johansson behind the scenes the  black widow costume was extremely tight  and hot like wearing sweaty pajamas the  heat became so bad that while filming  one scene she started hallucinating  johansson sweat so much that she would  wring her socks out at the end of the  shooting day her stunts were so  demanding that she shredded her costumes  and they had to be replaced every few  days  let me put you on hold the late chadwick  bozeman brought the black panther to  life portraying him as a stoic noble  leader while the character looks great  the black panther costume caused bozeman  some grief he felt suffocated by the  suit and it was so tight that it caused  him to have anxiety about wearing it it  is not breathable in order to  continuously wear the suit bozeman had  to get into a zen state in order to  remain calm in true bozeman fashion he  pushed through to deliver the iconic  character we now know dead  it's not the end in later movies robert  downey jr only had to wear some pads and  trackers for scenes involving iron man  suit however in the first iron man  downey donned a full ironman getup it  was a very stuffy uncomfortable and  restrictive suit when he had the helmet  on the led lights inside blinded him  luckily they didn't make him wear the  helmet for future films hey robert would  you mind putting on that helmet no yes  no gal gadot's wonder woman costume  looks amazing but it wasn't the most  comfortable to wear the corset was so  tight that gadot couldn't breathe and  she initially didn't say anything  because she was just so grateful to have  gotten the role in the first place  fortunately she got the costume loosened  for future films and was able to  continue fighting bad guys right before  i passed out they noticed that i was  breathing quite heavily christian bale  played batman for three movies and the  batsuit didn't feel as cool as it looked  he thought they should recast him during  the first movie i really did because it  was so claustrophobic that i didn't feel  like i could breathe i felt they've made  a mistake and i can't do this on top of  this he almost fainted while filming the  dark knight rises and i just put up with  it you know this is just a hell of an  honor really getting to wear this while  the beast we see on screen is completely  cgi dan stevens was actually on set  portraying the character he had to wear  a bulky suit and walk on stilts the very  physical role caused stevens to overheat  and sweat a ton subsequently leading to  weight loss i was physically  conditioning my legs to be on stilts for  12 hours a day and also conditioning the  rest of me so that i didn't waste away  to keep his weight from dipping too low  stevens had to eat a lot he stated that  he was eating up to four roast dinners a  day just to maintain his physicality  will you join me for dinner the makeup  and dressing process for vision is not  one we envy paul bettany had to wear a  skin-tight suit that extended over his  head and restricted his hearing they  eventually had to poke holes near his  ears so he could hear better on set it  takes about three and a half hours to  get into the suit but only 30 seconds to  rip it off according to betany there are  moments of such intense claustrophobia  in this thing oscar isaac had to wear an  elaborate ensemble of clothing to become  apocalypse on top of his blue makeup he  wore multiple prosthetics high-heeled  boots to push him over six feet tall and  a 40-pound suit it was hard for isaac to  move and breathe in the outfit i would  do some acting and then go to my tent  and try to breathe it was rough even  after all that isaac said the worst part  was getting it off as they had to scrape  the prosthetics off for hours apocalypse  that was excruciating catwoman is known  for wearing tight leather clothing but  it doesn't make for a comfortable  experience for the actresses that  portray the burglar when hathaway played  the character in 2012's the dark knight  rises she had a very difficult time with  the skin-tight costume it was a  challenge to breathe in and hathaway  described it as a psychological  terrorist i didn't understand how you  could be thin and strong i went into the  gym for 10 months and didn't come out  oops  ryan reynolds plays wade wilson aka the  wisecracking deadpool his suit was  nothing to laugh about though reynolds  had trouble breathing in the costume as  it was tight and hot they actually had  to redesign the first version of the  costume because it was way too tight for  reynold's body which he got in shape for  the movie i'm always so terrified i'll  like throw up in the mask or something  you know there's no space in that thing  at all  is the mask muffling my voice the live  action grinch movie starring jim carrey  has impressive makeup and costumes it  took eight hours to apply carrie's full  body makeup prosthetics and costume  which he described as being buried alive  each day he went through this grueling  process 92 times during the course of  filming the christmas flick they  actually brought in a cia operative to  train carrie to cope with torture so he  could continue playing the character  without having a complete meltdown and i  went back to my trailer and put my leg  through the wall and i told ron howard i  couldn't do the movie the winter  soldier's outfit may not seem like it's  too bad to wear but sebastian stan is  here to tell you otherwise the mask he  had to wear for most of the movie was  extremely restrictive to his breathing  to the point where he almost passed out  they shot a lot of his fight scenes in  june and july in the heat which made  things much worse i would just have to  literally rip it off my face and just  breathe so i gotta know how to breathe  right we already talked about one  catwoman so let's discuss another that  had a less than ideal costume michelle  pfeiffer played the character in 1992's  batman returns her iconic leather suit  was extremely problematic for pfeiffer  to wear and she said it was the most  uncomfortable costume she had ever worn  the face mask was smashing my face and  choking me to get the suit as tight as  it was they actually vacuum sealed it  onto pfeiffer meow margot robbie's  harley quinn is one of the dceu's most  popular characters we first saw her in  2016's suicide squad where she sported a  ripped t-shirt and very short shorts  robbie said she didn't like the costume  as it made her self-conscious on top of  this the tight shorts made it difficult  to eat and the t-shirt would get wet and  uncomfortably cling to her body director  david ayer didn't think denim overalls  would be appropriate for that character  luckily for margo she was able to ditch  these clothes in later films and was  just as amazing in the role  what although we like to imagine  ourselves in our favorite characters  outfit we don't envy these actors at all  despite how uncomfortable and difficult  it was they pushed through to deliver  performances that made it all worth it  so the next time you see a character  with an awesome costume on the big  screen consider what they had to go  through on set which costume do you  think would be the worst to wear

